rue] [17592186358121 1089 "q-127577" 13194139535625 true] [17592186358121 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535625 true] [17592186358121 1100 "The unit tangent vector to a curve at an arbitrary point is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}+1}\\cdot q(t).\n$$\n\nFind the principal normal vector at the point where $t=1$, if \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q(1)=-i+j+\\sqrt{2}\\,k,\\,{q}^{′}(1)=2\\,j+\\sqrt{2}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535625 true] [17592186358121 1113 #uuid "c57537a4-6650-5b6e-a37e-dea399e9f547" 13194139535625 true] [17592186358121 1145 "First, we calculate ${T}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}+1}\\cdot q(t)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}+1})\\cdot q(t)+\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}+1}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(q(t)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2t}{({t}^{2}+1)^{2}}\\cdot q(t)+\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}+1}\\cdot {q}^{′}(t) \\\\  \\\\ {T}^{′}(1) & =-\\frac{2(1)}{({1}^{2}+1)^{2}}\\cdot q(1)+\\frac{1}{{1}^{2}+1}\\cdot {q}^{′}(1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}(-i+j+\\sqrt{2}\\,k)+\\frac{1}{2}(2\\,j+\\sqrt{2}\\,k) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(i+j)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNext, we find the magnitude of ${T}^{′}(1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{T}^{′}(1)‖ & =|\\frac{1}{2}|\\sqrt{(1)^{2}+(1)^{2}+(0)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${T}^{′}(1)$ and obtain the principal normal to the curve at the point where $t=1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(1) & =\\frac{{T}^{′}(1)}{‖{T}^{′}(1)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{1}{2}(i+j)}{(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(i+j)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that when we find the scalar product of $N$ and $T$ at the point where $t=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(1)\\cdot N(1) & =\\frac{1}{2}q(1)\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(i+j) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-i+j+\\sqrt{2}\\,k)\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(i+j) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}(-1+1+0) \\\\  & =0.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535625 true] [175921